ning cards\n3. Prevent the landlord from playing out\n\nReason:\nWith the landlord at only 2 cards, this is a critical moment. I must play the BlackJoker to take control of the game. This high card will almost certainly win the trick (only RedJoker can beat it), allowing me to lead with my remaining low cards (♦4, ♣6) on subsequent turns. If I play a low card now, the landlord will likely take control and potentially win the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["BlackJoker"]}'}
